WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.120
The end of an epic nine-film arc, The Rise
of Skywalker has the near-impossible task

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:08.420
of wrapping up cinema's most-celebrated space
saga.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.790
Here are some fun production details to get
you pumped, plus some supposedly leaked plot

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:15.349
points that just might come into fruition.

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:18.000
WARNING: Major spoilers ahead ... potentially!

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.020
One new planet we'll be visiting in The Rise
of Skywalker is called Pasaana, a world of

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.840
sand and unforgiving sun.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.460
Yeah — another one.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.949
The planet, which is actually the Wadi Rum
desert valley in southern Jordan, will seemingly

00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:33.630
play host to a pivotal moment in The Rise
of Skywalker.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:38.860
We saw Rey jumping over a TIE fighter on a
very Jordanian-looking landscape in the first

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:42.820
Episode IX teaser trailer, as well as Finn
and Poe skidding on sand.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.480
At this stage, all we know for sure about
Pasaana is that it's home to the Aki-Aki,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.040
a native race being played by Jordanian locals.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:54.940
Rumors that red stormtroopers would be appearing
in The Rise of Skywalker had been doing the

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.930
rounds online for months before Lucasfilm
finally confirmed them.

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:03.660
According to StarWars.com, these fearsome-looking
soldiers are known as Sith troopers.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.539
But there's more going on here than just a
simple palette swap.

00:01:06.539 --> 00:01:12.450
Speaking for a feature on StarWars.com, Lucasfilm
archivist Madlyn Burkert broke down the Sith

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.530
trooper uniform, saying,

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.940
"It has some really unique aesthetics to it,
and it has some subtle ties to previous stormtrooper

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:21.340
designs, which I think fans will enjoy discovering."

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:26.740
Episode IX director J.J. Abrams seems equally
excited about the introduction of the Sith

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:30.630
troopers, saying that he cannot wait for fans
to meet this new batch of baddies.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:31.630
Abrams said,

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:35.799
"The materials, the color, the lines... there
is something about the aesthetic of it that

00:01:35.799 --> 00:01:37.439
just felt absolutely right."

00:01:37.439 --> 00:01:41.399
Who the Sith troopers serve remains a mystery
— some are convinced they'll do the bidding

00:01:41.399 --> 00:01:45.461
of the returning Emperor Palpatine, while
other sources report that they'll answer only

00:01:45.461 --> 00:01:46.240
to Kylo Ren.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:52.359
It's been reported by leakers and self-proclaimed
insiders that Rey will be getting a new lightsaber

00:01:52.359 --> 00:01:57.840
in The Rise of Skywalker — and if you believe
the special look teaser shown at D23, that

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.990
weapon might have more in common with Darth
Maul than Darth Vader.

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:01.990
"Ridiculous."

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:02.740
*Chewie noises*

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.909
"Shh. The grown-ups are talking."

00:02:04.909 --> 00:02:09.580
The footage drove the audience wild, according
to CinemaBlend, who spoke with Daisy Ridley

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.720
about the apparent dark side reveal.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:15.680
Ridley said she felt nervous about how the
footage would be received, but that, quote,

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.890
"hearing the audience reaction was amazing."

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:22.100
But the actress kept quiet when asked if viewers
should take the whole dark Rey thing at face

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.100
value.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:23.980
"Uhhhhhm…

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:25.440
I mean, we'll see."

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:31.190
Like many in Star Wars before her, new character
Zorii Bliss was first introduced by her looks

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:32.810
rather than her personality.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:35.360
Was she a hero, a villain, or a little of
both?

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.380
Either way, fans agreed on one thing: she
looked a lot like a rose gold version of Boba

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:39.940
Fett.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.900
A Vanity Fair feature described the dual-blaster-carrying
Bliss as a masked scoundrel who hangs out

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:49.920
in a disreputable place called the Thieves'
Quarter on the snowy planet of Kijimi.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:55.380
Actress Keri Russell has since revealed even
more info, describing her as a cool and shady

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.220
type, a criminal of sorts, and a friend of
Poe Dameron.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:02.860
She went into more detail when Variety spoke
to her and co-star Oscar Isaac.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:09.900
“She has a little bit of a checkered past,
and maybe some questionable morals, but really

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.020
she's an old friend of Poe's."

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.580
Does that mean Dameron and Bliss have a romantic
history?

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:16.480
Or did they just used to do star crimes together?

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:17.920
"It's complicated.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.520
Ehh, it's complicated."

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.460
Excited Twitter users are already stanning
their relationship — except for those who

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.680
are still holding on to hope for Finn and
Poe.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:30.500
Rumors that The Rise of Skywalker would go
out of its way to tie all the previous Star

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:34.090
Wars movies together have been floating around
for a couple of years now.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:38.150
The specifics of this overarching connection
remain a mystery, but from the little we've

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:42.320
seen of the movie so far, it's clear the movie
isn't skimping on nostalgia.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:47.680
This theme of bringing it all together was
central at D23 Expo 2019, where a sizzle reel

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:51.230
featuring iconic shots from throughout the
series was screened.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:54.910
While The Force Awakens and The Last Jedi
have already done quite a bit to call back

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:59.130
to the original trilogy, fans can now hope
that the mysteries of Star Wars might come

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:04.210
full circle, exploring questions and bringing
back story material that was first introduced

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:05.680
in the prequel trilogy.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:06.940
But it's probably not midichlorians.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:09.080
And it's hopefully not this guy, either.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.820
Have we really seen the last of Harrison Ford's
Han Solo?

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.340
Some people don't think so.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.980
It's been reported for awhile that Han will
appear as a Force ghost in The Rise of Skywalker

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:21.489
and help turn his son back to the light.

00:04:21.489 --> 00:04:26.479
This comes by way of JediPaxis, a Redditor
and moderator of the StarWarsLeaks forum,

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:31.760
who claims to have compiled a detailed breakdown
of Episode IX via various inside sources.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:35.240
Lots of people think it's true, but take it
with a grain of salt and all that.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:39.780
According to the leak, Kylo Ren and Rey will
engage in an epic lightsaber battle on the

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.150
wreckage of the second Death Star, from which
Rey will emerge triumphant.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:49.080
It's in that moment of defeat for Kylo that
Han will reportedly appear and coax his wayward

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:49.780
son back to the light.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:50.780
Shocking, huh?

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:52.520
"What are you talking about?"

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:57.370
That said, plenty of fans are scratching their
heads about how exactly a Han "Force" ghost

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:02.069
would work, especially since the only Force
we ever saw that guy using was garden-variety

00:05:02.069 --> 00:05:03.090
lethal force.

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:07.479
While many are convinced that Kylo Ren is
in for a redemption arc, mirroring his grandfather's

00:05:07.479 --> 00:05:11.569
last-minute change of heart in Return of the
Jedi, fans are having a hard time believing

00:05:11.569 --> 00:05:14.300
Han will be the one to do it, no matter what
a leak says.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:19.040
Some are theorizing that the leaked Han detail
may be "Obi-Wan killed your father" style

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:23.439
misdirection, and that the real movie will
see Anakin himself appear as a Force ghost

00:05:23.439 --> 00:05:25.740
— but there's not much evidence out there
for that yet.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:29.980
Either way, it's looking pretty likely that
Ben Solo won't finish this series as a bad

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:30.520
guy.

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:34.640
What was up with C-3PO's red eyes in that
D23 footage?

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:38.620
Well, apparently, it's a long story, and a
pretty sad one, as well.

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:43.840
If leaks are to be believed, our heroes discover
a dagger on Pasaana with a message engraved

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:45.849
on it that none of them can understand.

00:05:45.849 --> 00:05:49.949
Even C-3PO can't translate it because of limitations
in his programming.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:54.759
Eventually, Poe Dameron intervenes, claiming
to have a contact that can help 3PO translate

00:05:54.759 --> 00:05:57.870
the ancient writing: Keri Russell's Zorii
Bliss.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:02.009
Russell's character introduces the gang to
an alien friend of hers who knows how to unlock

00:06:02.009 --> 00:06:02.580
the message.

00:06:03.009 --> 00:06:07.879
But, if rumors about the plot of Episode IX
are indeed true, our heroes face a huge dilemma

00:06:07.879 --> 00:06:09.539
involving their beloved droid.

00:06:09.539 --> 00:06:12.819
Is red-eyed C-3PO what happens after he cracks
the code?

00:06:12.819 --> 00:06:13.949
Is he forever altered?

00:06:13.949 --> 00:06:16.009
Or do our heroes find another way?

00:06:16.009 --> 00:06:17.220
We'll have to wait and see.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:22.479
Rumor has it that the true extent of Rey's
powers will be revealed in The Rise of Skywalker,

00:06:22.479 --> 00:06:27.169
and one previously unknown ability will come
to the fore pretty early on in the movie.

00:06:27.169 --> 00:06:31.830
After the heroes meet up with Lando on Pasaana,
they supposedly end up in a series of underground

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:32.360
tunnels.

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:36.420
These tunnels in the desert were created by
a huge sand creature, who isn't particularly

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:37.960
pleased with their intrusion.

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:39.560
At least, not to begin with.

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:43.940
The crew look like they're done for when the
creature corners them, but, according to leaks,

00:06:43.949 --> 00:06:47.229
Rey uses a new Force power which allows our
heroes to escape.

00:06:47.229 --> 00:06:51.230
The exact nature of this power and it’s
implications we'll leave a mystery, but Rey

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:57.220
also reportedly uses this newfound power in
a later scene, with far, far greater consequences.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:02.360
The rumor that General Hux will be revealed
as a mole in The Rise of Skywalker is more

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:06.630
than a year old now, so even if you believe
nothing else from the movie's many alleged

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:09.370
leaks, this detail may indeed be legit.

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:13.949
The rivalry between Hux and Kylo Ren has been
steadily building over the course of the previous

00:07:13.949 --> 00:07:18.819
two films, reaching a critical turning point
when Kylo took out Snoke and assumed control

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:20.020
of the First Order.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:24.660
According to leaked plot details, it's revealed
pretty early on in Episode IX that the Resistance

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:28.460
has been dealing with an alien informant who
has been acting as a middle man between a

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:30.940
certain First Order mole and our heroes.

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:35.469
If you buy the legitimacy of the leaks, Hux
is revealed to be the mole at a critical juncture.

00:07:35.469 --> 00:07:40.620
But, as they say, no good deed goes unpunished,
so it's likely that Hux's betrayal will have

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:44.840
some serious repercussions … if this whole
"Hux the Mole" gossip even turns out to be

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:45.640
true.

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:51.460
The news that Billy Dee Williams was reprising
his iconic Star Wars role in The Rise of Skywalker

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:53.680
was huge for fans of the original trilogy.

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:58.380
Since the announcement, people have been theorizing
about what Lando Calrissian could have been

00:07:58.389 --> 00:08:00.479
doing since we last saw him.

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:04.599
According to leaked plot details, Lando has
been laying low on Pasaana, the sandy world

00:08:04.599 --> 00:08:08.839
that's set to feature prominently in the final
installment of the Skywalker saga.

00:08:08.839 --> 00:08:13.190
It's also rumored that Lando reveals to the
heroes that he's the father of a child, one

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:15.080
who was taken away from him at an early age.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:19.479
It's long been theorized that Naomi Ackie's
Jannah is the daughter of Lando Calrissian.

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:24.820
The new character was revealed at Star Wars
Celebration 2019, and fans couldn't help but

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:28.960
notice that her blue and yellow costume, complete
with a cape, looks an awful lot like Calrissian's

00:08:28.969 --> 00:08:30.809
get-up from the original trilogy.

00:08:30.809 --> 00:08:33.680
"Hello, what have we here?"

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:41.160
Speculation surrounding Rey's parents has
been rife ever since Kylo Ren told her that

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:41.620
they were nothing but "filthy junk traders"
in The Last Jedi.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:45.820
Some fans were convinced that the hero of
the sequel trilogy had Skywalker blood running

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:50.950
through her veins, and when the title of Episode
IX was revealed, many believed that J.J. Abrams

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:52.420
planned to do some retconning.

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:56.580
However, according to the latest leaks, The
Rise of Skywalker will reveal that Rey is

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:59.100
actually the granddaughter of Emperor Palpatine.

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:03.520
It might sound far-fetched, but it would explain
why the Force is so strong with her.

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:07.329
The rumors say that Rey's parents were killed
on Jakku because they tried to conceal her

00:09:07.329 --> 00:09:08.800
from Sith loyalists.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:11.840
This would mean that Palpatine fathered a
child at some stage.

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:13.200
Is this possible?

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:18.460
Well, George Lucas' abandoned TV show, Star
Wars: Underworld, did plan to reveal that

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:21.880
Palpatine once had his heart broken by a woman
with ties to criminal gangs on Coruscant.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:25.600
It would be a pretty bold move for the story
to take, that's for sure.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:31.040
A great deal of the Rise of Skywalker chatter
has centered around Emperor Palpatine ever

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:33.080
since the debut of the teaser trailer.

00:09:33.089 --> 00:09:37.610
He didn't appear in the teaser, but his infamous
evil cackle did, and to make sure there was

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:42.220
no misunderstanding about what that meant,
actor Ian McDiarmid appeared on stage right

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:45.940
after the footage premiered at Star Wars Celebration
2019.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:49.579
We didn't get a full-on shot of Palpatine
in the final trailer, either, but the character

00:09:49.579 --> 00:09:51.899
was a much bigger presence this time around.

00:09:51.899 --> 00:09:56.330
We do, however, get a shot of his new throne
in the final trailer — only it isn't a new

00:09:56.330 --> 00:09:57.480
throne at all.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:02.500
This imposing, jagged structure was actually
inspired by an old sketch that legendary concept

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:06.970
artist Ralph McQuarrie drew when he was working
on Return of the Jedi.

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:12.259
Lucasfilm's creative art manager Phil Szostak
pointed this out on Twitter, using a side-by-side

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:16.760
comparison to show how the throne in McQuarrie's
sketch and the one in the movie are basically

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:17.660
identical.

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:20.580
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:24.460
Plus, even more Looper videos about the Skywalker
saga are coming soon.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:28.680
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

